   <condition type="2">
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EBRD is supporting the project to modernise and upgrade the water and  wastewater services in the city of Nurek in Tajikistan. The EBRD would provide  a loan of up to USD 2.5 million to the Nurek Water Company, the municipal  company owned by the municipality of Nurek. The Republic of Tajikistan would  provide a sovereign guarantee. Nurek City, as owner of the Nurek Water Company,  would sign a Project Support Agreement with the Bank. The EBRD will also seek  an investment grant from an international donor of USD 2.5 million for  this urgently needed water and wastewater infrastructure rehabilitation project.  The overall objectives of this project are to: (a) rehabilitate the water  supply and selected wastewater improvements; and (b) improve financial and  operational management of the Nurek Water Company. For more details, please refer to the project summary document at https://www.ebrd.com/view/psd/47398</narrative>
   </condition>
